# WHERE THIS FILE HAS TO LIVE, AND WHY IT IS NOT IN deploy/.
#
# deploy/docker-compose.yml builds the api with `context: ..`, so the build
# context is the REPOSITORY ROOT. Docker reads .dockerignore from the context
# root and nowhere else: a copy beside the Dockerfile in deploy/ is read by
# nothing, silently. Before this file existed BuildKit reported
# `load .dockerignore / transferring context: 2B` — the empty default.
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR. deploy/Dockerfile stage 1 does `COPY . .`, so without this
# every git-ignored file in the tree lands in the BUILD stage — including
# deploy/.env, the file .gitignore exists to keep out of the repository and
# .env.example tells developers to create. Measured: a canary
# `POSTGRES_PASSWORD=` line written into deploy/.env came back out of
# `docker run --entrypoint /bin/cat <buildstage> /src/deploy/.env`.
#
# The SHIPPED image is unaffected either way — stage 2 is scratch and copies
# exactly two paths — so this is intermediate-image and build-cache exposure,
# not a leak in what ships. It is also a cache fix: `.git` (5.1 MB) and the
# stray `./api` binary (9.2 MB) invalidated `COPY . .` on every commit.
#
# Nothing the build needs may be added here: go.mod, go.sum, cmd/ and internal/
# are what stage 1 compiles.

# Secrets and local environment. deploy/.env.example is checked in and IS
# wanted in the context (it documents the knobs); deploy/.env never is.
deploy/.env
.env

# Version control and its history.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Build output. `/api` is what `go build ./...` — the first command of
# `make check` — leaves in the current directory on every run.
/api
/bin/
/out/

# Go test artefacts.
*.test
*.out

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
